Side-by-side
The same statement (a barangay’s English label) in all three formats, as actually shipped in 2023-10-24/. Turtle is compact with prefix declarations; N-Triples is fully expanded and line-oriented; the JSON-LD is shipped in expanded form (full URIs, no @context).
Turtle (delta.ttl):
@prefix skos: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#&gt; .

&lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/entity/1381500036&gt; skos:prefLabel "Rizal"@en .
N-Triples (delta.nt) — every term fully spelled out:
&lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/entity/1381500036&gt; &lt;http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel&gt; "Rizal"@en .
JSON-LD (delta.jsonld) — expanded, one node per object:
{
  "@id": "https://psgc.gov.ph/entity/1381500036",
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
    { "@language": "en", "@value": "Rizal" }
  ]
}

SPARQL recipes
All three queries run against the committed YYYY-MM-DD/delta.ttl files. They use the predicates actually emitted — see Entity & event URIs for the shapes.
1. List every creation event in a snapshot. The event type is an org:classification link to a psgc:concept/change-type/... concept:
prefix org:  &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/org#&gt;
prefix dct:  &lt;http://purl.org/dc/terms/&gt;
prefix psgc: &lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/&gt;

select ?event ?desc where {
  ?event a org:ChangeEvent ;
         org:classification psgc:concept/change-type/creation ;
         dct:description ?desc .
}
order by ?event
2. Trace an entity’s history across snapshots via its correspondence code. The 9-digit correspondence code (the identity that survives PSGC re-codings) is carried as a typed literal; org:originalOrganization/org:resultingOrganization link the two codes:
prefix org:  &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/org#&gt;
prefix psgc: &lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/&gt;
prefix xsd:  &lt;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#&gt;

select ?ev ?entity ?code where {
  ?entity org:identifier "137602033"^^psgc:correspondence-code ;
          org:identifier ?code .
  filter(str(?code) != "137602033")   # the 10-digit PSGC code, not the correspondence code
  # which code_change events touch this correspondence code (the event URI embeds the snapshot date)
  ?ev org:originalOrganization|org:resultingOrganization ?entity .
}
order by ?ev
3. Count events by type per snapshot. When several snapshots are loaded into one graph, group by the dct:date on each event and the change-type concept:
prefix org: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/org#&gt;
prefix dct: &lt;http://purl.org/dc/terms/&gt;

select ?date ?type (count(?ev) as ?n) where {
  ?ev a org:ChangeEvent ;
      dct:date ?date ;
      org:classification ?typeConcept .
  bind(strafter(str(?typeConcept), "change-type/") as ?type)
}
group by ?date ?type
order by ?date ?type

Worked examples
Pulled verbatim from 2023-10-24/delta.ttl.
Entity URI. A barangay that was created in this snapshot — note both the 10-digit PSGC code and the 9-digit correspondence code on org:identifier, the name on skos:prefLabel, and its level (Bgy) plus urban/rural classification as org:classification concepts:
&lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/entity/1381500036&gt; a org:OrganizationalUnit ;
    dct:date "2023-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
    schema1:population 15103 ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rizal"@en ;
    org:classification &lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/concept/geographic-level/Bgy&gt;,
        &lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/concept/urban-rural/U&gt; ;
    org:identifier "137602033"^^xsd:string,
        "1381500036"^^xsd:string,
        "137602033"^^psgc:correspondence-code .
Creation event URI. A creation carries only the resulting organization:
&lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/event/2023-10-24/0000&gt; a org:ChangeEvent ;
    dct:date "2023-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Aniban 1 (Bgy) created"@en ;
    org:classification &lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/concept/change-type/creation&gt; ;
    org:resultingOrganization &lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/entity/0402103076&gt; .
Code-change event URI. A re-coding carries both the original and the resulting entity, so a consumer can follow the identity from old code to new:
&lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/event/2023-10-24/0082&gt; a org:ChangeEvent ;
    dct:date "2023-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "PSGC code changed from 1380300033 to 1381500036"@en ;
    org:classification &lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/concept/change-type/code_change&gt; ;
    org:originalOrganization &lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/entity/1380300033&gt; ;
    org:resultingOrganization &lt;https://psgc.gov.ph/entity/1381500036&gt; .
Transfer / source provenance. There are no PROV-O triples in the committed deltas linking events to their PSA press release — the builder supports dct:source (legal basis) and prov:generatedAtTime (effective date) but the source data does not populate them. Until that gap closes, trace an event to its snapshot by the dct:date and the date embedded in the event URI (/event/2023-10-24/...). See Change-event types › Known limitations.

